  "notes": "Composed of {交|こう} (intersect, exchange) and ⟦{尾|び}→尾：18068_bi⟧ (tail). Literally \"crossing tails.\" A scientific, neutral term used exclusively for animals — never for humans in standard usage. Common in biology textbooks, nature documentaries, and wildlife observation contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {交尾|こうび}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to mate\n- {交尾|こうび}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{時期|じき}→時期：03269_jiki⟧: mating season\n- {交尾|こうび}⟦{行動|こうどう}→行動：02728_koudou⟧: mating behavior\n- {交尾|こうび}⟦{相手|あいて}→相手：01677_aite⟧: mating partner\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- つがい: mating pair — refers to a bonded pair of animals, often birds\n- ⟦{繁殖|はんしょく}→繁殖：08671_hanshoku⟧: breeding, reproduction — broader term covering the whole reproductive process including raising young\n- ⟦{生殖|せいしょく}→生殖：27947_seishoku⟧: reproduction — the biological process; more technical and scientific",
